how to fix the following code in TS:
class A<T> {
  a: T
}

In TypeScript, the error is likely because `a` has no initializer under `strictPropertyInitialization`.

Fix it by initializing `a`, usually via a constructor:

```ts
class A<T> {
  a: T;

  constructor(a: T) {
    this.a = a;
  }
}
```

Usage:

```ts
const x = new A<number>(123);
```

Other possible fixes:

```ts
class A<T> {
  a!: T; // definite assignment assertion
}
```

or:

```ts
class A<T> {
  a?: T; // may be undefined
}
```

Best option is usually the constructor version.
